response_text:
Use digit DP: let f(s) be the number of integers in [0, s] whose digit sum lies in [min_sum, max_sum]. The answer is f(num2) − f(num1) + (1 if num1 itself is good, else 0).

To compute f(s), walk the digits left to right with state (position, current digit sum, tight), where "tight" means the prefix so far equals the prefix of s:
- If tight, the next digit can go up to the current digit of s; otherwise up to 9.
- Prune any branch whose digit sum exceeds max_sum.
- At the end of the string, count 1 if the sum is at least min_sum.

Leading zeros need no special handling, since they don't change the digit sum. The number 0 has sum 0, which is below min_sum (at least 1), so it is never counted.

