1. For each value, record the index of its last occurrence.
2. Scan the array from left to right, keeping `reach`, the farthest last-occurrence index among the values seen so far.
3. When the current index `i` equals `reach`, every value seen so far has no copies to the right. So index `i` closes an independent block, and a cut after it is allowed.
4. Let `k` be the number of such blocks. Between consecutive blocks there are `k - 1` boundaries. Each one can independently be cut or not.
5. The answer is therefore `2^(k-1) mod (10^9 + 7)`.

