Split the word into blocks of length k, starting at indices 0, k, 2k, and so on. There are n/k blocks.

Each operation rewrites one block as a copy of another block. To make the word k-periodic, every block must end up equal to the same string. The cheapest choice is to keep the most common block unchanged and overwrite every other block with it. That takes one operation per block that differs from it.

So the answer is the number of blocks minus the count of the most frequent block.

