A number has exactly 2 proper divisors only when it has exactly 3 divisors in total. That happens exactly when the number is p² for some prime p, with divisors 1, p and p².

So the plan is:
1. Sieve all primes up to √(10⁹) ≈ 31623.
2. Count the primes p with l ≤ p² ≤ r. These are the special numbers in the range.
