Since the string has at most 250 characters, an O(n²) brute force is fast enough.

For each starting index `i`, extend the substring one character at a time:
- If the character is a vowel, add it to a set of vowels seen so far.
- Otherwise, increase the consonant count. Once the count exceeds `k`, stop extending from this `i`.
- Whenever the set holds all 5 vowels and the consonant count is exactly `k`, count the substring.

