- **Transition:** a path reaches (i, j) from above or from the left. If the XOR before entering (i, j) was `p`, it becomes `p ^ grid[i][j]`. So for each `p`, add the counts from the top and left neighbours into `dp[i][j][p ^ grid[i][j]]`.
