- the gaps between meetings, `startTime[i] - endTime[i-1]`;
- the gap after the last meeting, `eventTime - endTime[-1]`.

Since k ≤ n, the window size k+1 is at most n+1, so it always fits. A sliding window over the gaps finds the best sum in O(n).

