The approach is a greedy subsequence check.

1. Convert T to lowercase.
2. Scan S from left to right, matching characters of T in order. If all 3 characters are matched, T is a subsequence of S, so the answer is Yes.
3. Otherwise, if the last character of T is 'X', check whether the first 2 characters of T form a subsequence of S. If they do, the answer is Yes.
4. In all other cases, the answer is No.

Each check is a single pass over S, so the running time is linear in the length of S.

