      - Step up and go left along row r−1: (r−1, c+K+1) .. (r−1, c+1).
      - Finish at (r, c+1).
    - The final red (r, c+1) is adjacent to the first blue (r, c).
    - Blues use only rows ≥ r. The red squares in row r are at columns ≥ c+1, where no blue lies. So nothing overlaps.

